assumes the test runs from its package directory, which `go test` guarantees. And if the source file has syntax errors, `BuildBinary` will legitimately fail with a compilation error, which is the correct behavior.\n\nNow I'm verifying that `resolvePackageName` correctly handles the relative path `../../cmd/version` when called from the test's working directory...\n\nActually, I need to be careful here. The function returns `filepath.Base(\"../../cmd/version\")` which gives `\"version\"`, so the binary naming should work correctly. I've thought through all the edge cases now—the path resolution, the file existence check, the binary naming—and I'm ready to write the actual implementation with proper requirement references in the comments.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":152340,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":152340},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6fa6a34-6b72-48df-9ad8-34a9f8758a8b","uuid":"e811d9be-f565-4359-b19c-5885895e851c"}
