{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via an automated cobbler orchestrator) requested implementation of task #5121: create `pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go` containing tests for the differential testing harness. The task has four requirements (R1-R4) covering matching outputs, divergent outputs, normalizers, and BuildBinary. Three acceptance criteria must be met: tests pass with `go test ./pkg/testutils/... -count=1`, tests cover all four areas, and tests skip gracefully when cmd/ source is absent during generation runs. Git is managed externally - no git commands allowed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: run Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, compare stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - Subprocess test pattern: for testing t.Fatalf behavior, spawn test binary as subprocess via `os.Args[0]` with env var guard\n   - NormalizeFunc type alias: `func([]byte) []byte` for output normalization before comparison\n   - TimestampNormalizer: replaces syslog (`May 13 14:30:00`), ISO (`2026-05-13 14:30:00`), and time-only (`14:30:00`) patterns with `<TIMESTAMP>`\n   - ComposeNormalizers: chains multiple NormalizeFuncs in order\n   - BuildBinary: compiles Go package within module, returns executable path\n   - buildEnv: merges test env with process env, always sets `LC_ALL=C`\n   - formatDivergence: outputs \"divergence detected\" with args, stdin, ref/go stdout, ref/go stderr, ref/go exit code\n   - Generation-run graceful skip: check for main.go existence before building cmd/ binaries\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (existing, provided inline in project_context):\n     - Core harness implementation with RunDiffTests, DiffTest struct, compareOutputs, formatDivergence\n     - Key: `compareOutputs` compares `goRes` vs `refRes` for stdout, stderr, exit code equality\n     - Key: `formatDivergence` produces message with \"divergence detected\", \"ref stdout:\", \"go  stdout:\", \"ref exit:\", \"go  exit:\"\n     - Key: `buildEnv` always sets `envMap[\"LC_ALL\"] = \"C\"`\n     - Full source is in the conversation above (lines 1-239)\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/build.go` (existing, provided inline):\n     - BuildBinary(t, dir) calls `go build -o binPath dir`, returns path, fatals on failure\n     - resolvePackageName handles \".\" vs other paths via filepath.Base\n     - Full source is in the conversation above (lines 1-38)\n\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd001-testutils.yaml` (read first 80 lines):\n     - Defines DiffTest struct requirements (R1.1-R1.4)\n     - Documents canonical usage pattern for cmd/ test files\n     - Goals G1-G4: execution, comparison, normalization, go test integration\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go` (TO BE CREATED - not yet written):\n     - This is the deliverable file for task #5121\n     - Planned implementation detailed in section 8 below\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - the file has not been written or compiled. Only planning/analysis was completed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved the approach for testing t.Fatalf behavior: use subprocess test pattern with `exec.Command(os.Args[0], \"-test.run=^TestName$\")` and env var guard\n   - Solved the binary discovery problem: findBinary helper checks multiple paths (/bin/X, /usr/bin/X) and calls t.Skip if not found\n   - Solved subprocess skip safety: find binaries BEFORE the env var check so parent skips (never spawns subprocess) if binaries missing, preventing false passes in subprocess\n   - Solved the \"unused variable in parent path\" concern: Go compiler only requires variables to be used somewhere in the function (the if-block satisfies this)\n   - Identified that `ExitCode` field on DiffTest is not used in compareOutputs (it compares go vs ref, not against expected)\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full task specification with role, repository_files, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts. This is the primary work request.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go` with all planned test functions\n   - Run `go test ./pkg/testutils/... -count=1` to verify AC1\n   - Verify AC2 (coverage of matching, divergent, normalizers, BuildBinary)\n   - Verify AC3 (graceful skip when cmd/ source absent)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was about to write the file `pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go`. I had completed extensive analysis and planning but had NOT yet created the file. The planned implementation is:\n\n   ```go\n   // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n   // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n   package testutils\n\n   import (\n   \t\"bytes\"\n   \t\"os\"\n   \t\"os/exec\"\n   \t\"path/filepath\"\n   \t\"strings\"\n   \t\"testing\"\n   )\n\n   func findBinary(t *testing.T, name string, paths ...string) string {\n   \tt.Helper()\n   \tfor _, p := range paths {\n   \t\tif _, err := os.Stat(p); err == nil {\n   \t\t\treturn p\n   \t\t}\n   \t}\n   \tt.Skipf(\"%s binary not found\", name)\n   \treturn \"\"\n   }\n\n   func verifySubprocessFails(\n   \tt *testing.T, testName, envVar string, wantMsgs ...string,\n   ) {\n   \tt.Helper()\n   \tcmd := exec.Command(os.Args[0], \"-test.run=^\"+testName+\"$\")\n   \tcmd.Env = append(os.Environ(), envVar+\"=1\")\n   \toutput, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n   \tif err == nil {\n   \t\tt.Fatal(\"expected subprocess test to fail, but it passed\")\n   \t}\n   \tout := string(output)\n   \tfor _, msg := range wantMsgs {\n   \t\tif !strings.Contains(out, msg) {\n   \t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"expected %q in output, got:\\n%s\", msg, out)\n   \t\t}\n   \t}\n   }\n\n   // R1: matching binaries produce no test failures.\n   func TestRunDiffTests_MatchingOutputs(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \techoBin := findBinary(t, \"echo\", \"/bin/echo\", \"/usr/bin/echo\")\n   \ttests := []DiffTest{\n   \t\t{Name: \"simple-arg\", Args: []string{\"hello\"}},\n   \t\t{Name: \"multiple-args\", Args: []string{\"hello\", \"world\"}},\n   \t\t{Name: \"no-args\"},\n   \t}\n   \tRunDiffTests(t, echoBin, echoBin, tests)\n   }\n\n   // R1: matching exit codes produce no test failures.\n   func TestRunDiffTests_MatchingExitCodes(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \ttrueBin := findBinary(t, \"true\", \"/usr/bin/true\", \"/bin/true\")\n   \tfalseBin := findBinary(t, \"false\", \"/usr/bin/false\", \"/bin/false\")\n   \tRunDiffTests(t, trueBin, trueBin, []DiffTest{\n   \t\t{Name: \"true-zero-exit\"},\n   \t})\n   \tRunDiffTests(t, falseBin, falseBin, []DiffTest{\n   \t\t{Name: \"false-nonzero-exit\"},\n   \t})\n   }\n\n   // R1: matching stdin passthrough produces no test failures.\n   func TestRunDiffTests_WithStdin(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \tcatBin := findBinary(t, \"cat\", \"/bin/cat\", \"/usr/bin/cat\")\n   \ttests := []DiffTest{\n   \t\t{Name: \"passthrough\", Stdin: []byte(\"hello from stdin\\n\")},\n   \t\t{Name: \"empty-stdin\", Stdin: []byte{}},\n   \t\t{Name: \"multiline\", Stdin: []byte(\"line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n\")},\n   \t}\n   \tRunDiffTests(t, catBin, catBin, tests)\n   }\n\n   // R1: matching env-var output produces no test failures.\n   func TestRunDiffTests_WithEnv(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \tbin := findBinary(t, \"printenv\", \"/usr/bin/printenv\", \"/bin/printenv\")\n   \ttests := []DiffTest{\n   \t\t{Name: \"lc-all-default\", Args: []string{\"LC_ALL\"}},\n   \t\t{\n   \t\t\tName: \"custom-env\",\n   \t\t\tArgs: []string{\"DIFFTEST_CUSTOM\"},\n   \t\t\tEnv:  []string{\"DIFFTEST_CUSTOM=test_value\"},\n   \t\t},\n   \t}\n   \tRunDiffTests(t, bin, bin, tests)\n   }\n\n   // R2: stdout divergence is reported with diagnostic output.\n   func TestRunDiffTests_DivergentStdout(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \techoBin := findBinary(t, \"echo\", \"/bin/echo\", \"/usr/bin/echo\")\n   \ttrueBin := findBinary(t, \"true\", \"/usr/bin/true\", \"/bin/true\")\n   \tif os.Getenv(\"TEST_DIVERGENT_STDOUT\") == \"1\" {\n   \t\tRunDiffTests(t, echoBin, trueBin, []DiffTest{\n   \t\t\t{Name: \"stdout-differs\", Args: []string{\"hello\"}},\n   \t\t})\n   \t\treturn\n   \t}\n   \tverifySubprocessFails(t, \"TestRunDiffTests_DivergentStdout\",\n   \t\t\"TEST_DIVERGENT_STDOUT\",\n   \t\t\"divergence detected\", \"ref stdout\", \"go  stdout\")\n   }\n\n   // R2: exit-code divergence is reported with diagnostic output.\n   func TestRunDiffTests_DivergentExitCode(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \ttrueBin := findBinary(t, \"true\", \"/usr/bin/true\", \"/bin/true\")\n   \tfalseBin := findBinary(t, \"false\", \"/usr/bin/false\", \"/bin/false\")\n   \tif os.Getenv(\"TEST_DIVERGENT_EXIT\") == \"1\" {\n   \t\tRunDiffTests(t, trueBin, falseBin, []DiffTest{\n   \t\t\t{Name: \"exit-code-differs\"},\n   \t\t})\n   \t\treturn\n   \t}\n   \tverifySubprocessFails(t, \"TestRunDiffTests_DivergentExitCode\",\n   \t\t\"TEST_DIVERGENT_EXIT\",\n   \t\t\"divergence detected\", \"ref exit\", \"go  exit\")\n   }\n\n   // R3: TimestampNormalizer replaces timestamps with placeholder.\n   func TestTimestampNormalizer(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \ttests := []struct {\n   \t\tname  string\n   \t\tinput string\n   \t\twant  string\n   \t}{\n   \t\t{\"syslog-format\", \"May 13 14:30:00 message\", \"<TIMESTAMP> message\"},\n   \t\t{\"iso-format\", \"2026-05-13 14:30:00 message\", \"<TIMESTAMP> message\"},\n   \t\t{\"time-only\", \"14:30:00 message\", \"<TIMESTAMP> message\"},\n   \t\t{\"no-timestamp\", \"hello world\", \"hello world\"},\n   \t\t{\"empty\", \"\", \"\"},\n   \t\t{\"embedded\", \"event at 09:15:30 done\", \"event at <TIMESTAMP> done\"},\n   \t}\n   \tfor _, tc := range tests {\n   \t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n   \t\t\tt.Parallel()\n   \t\t\tgot := string(TimestampNormalizer([]byte(tc.input)))\n   \t\t\tif got != tc.want {\n   \t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"got %q, want %q\", got, tc.want)\n   \t\t\t}\n   \t\t})\n   \t}\n   }\n\n   // R3: ComposeNormalizers applies functions in order.\n   func TestComposeNormalizers(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \tupper := func(b []byte) []byte { return bytes.ToUpper(b) }\n   \tprefix := func(b []byte) []byte {\n   \t\treturn append([]byte(\">>\"), b...)\n   \t}\n   \tcomposed := ComposeNormalizers(upper, prefix)\n   \tgot := string(composed([]byte(\"hello\")))\n   \tif got != \">>HELLO\" {\n   \t\tt.Fatalf(\"got %q, want %q\", got, \">>HELLO\")\n   \t}\n   }\n\n   // R3: ComposeNormalizers with no functions is identity.\n   func TestComposeNormalizers_Empty(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \tcomposed := ComposeNormalizers()\n   \tgot := string(composed([]byte(\"unchanged\")))\n   \tif got != \"unchanged\" {\n   \t\tt.Fatalf(\"got %q, want %q\", got, \"unchanged\")\n   \t}\n   }\n\n   // R4: BuildBinary compiles a valid cmd/ package.\n   func TestBuildBinary(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \tmainFile := filepath.Join(\"..\", \"..\", \"cmd\", \"version\", \"main.go\")\n   \tif _, err := os.Stat(mainFile); os.IsNotExist(err) {\n   \t\tt.Skip(\"cmd/version not yet generated\")\n   \t}\n   \tbinPath := BuildBinary(t, \"../../cmd/version\")\n   \tinfo, err := os.Stat(binPath)\n   \tif err != nil {\n   \t\tt.Fatalf(\"binary does not exist: %v\", err)\n   \t}\n   \tif info.Mode()&0o111 == 0 {\n   \t\tt.Fatal(\"binary is not executable\")\n   \t}\n   }\n\n   // R4: BuildBinary fails on non-existent package.\n   func TestBuildBinary_Failure(t *testing.T) {\n   \tt.Parallel()\n   \tif os.Getenv(\"TEST_BUILD_FAILURE\") == \"1\" {\n   \t\tBuildBinary(t, \"./nonexistent-pkg-abc123\")\n   \t\treturn\n   \t}\n   \tverifySubprocessFails(t, \"TestBuildBinary_Failure\",\n   \t\t\"TEST_BUILD_FAILURE\", \"BuildBinary\")\n   }\n   ```\n\n   Key design considerations already resolved:\n   - System binaries found before subprocess env var check to prevent false passes if binary missing in subprocess\n   - All functions under 40-line limit per E8\n   - t.Parallel() on all tests (safe - no os.Chdir, no global state mutation)\n   - t.Helper() on all helper functions\n   - Table-driven tests for TimestampNormalizer\n   - Copyright header on file\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the file `pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go` with the planned implementation above using the Write tool, then run `go test ./pkg/testutils/... -count=1` to verify all acceptance criteria pass. This directly continues the task from the user's original request: \"Follow these steps in order... 3. **Implement** — Complete the work described in Requirements and Files to Create/Modify.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5121/a6fa6a34-6b72-48df-9ad8-34a9f8758a8b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6fa6a34-6b72-48df-9ad8-34a9f8758a8b","uuid":"b4bcb97b-47ea-41b1-81e8-8cf0406a5bdb","timestamp":"2026-05-14T02:17:08.609Z","isSynthetic":true}
